  "content": "<div id=\"readability-page-1\" class=\"page\"><div id=\"\"> <p>APOD</p> <p>Astronomy Picture of the Day</p> <p> <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/archive/\">Discover the cosmos!</a> Each day a different image or photograph of our fascinating universe is featured, along with a brief explanation written by a professional astronomer. </p> <div><p><img width=\"2060\" height=\"1393\" src=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSP.jpg?w=2060&amp;h=1393&amp;fit=clip&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\" alt=\"Two people are seated looking up at the night sky.\" decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSP.jpg?w=2060&amp;h=1393&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 2060w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSP.jpg?w=300&amp;h=203&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 300w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSP.jpg?w=768&amp;h=519&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 768w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSP.jpg?w=1024&amp;h=692&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1024w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSP.jpg?w=1536&amp;h=1039&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1536w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSP.jpg?w=2048&amp;h=1385&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 2048w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSP.jpg?w=400&amp;h=270&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 400w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSP.jpg?w=600&amp;h=406&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 600w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSP.jpg?w=900&amp;h=609&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 900w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSP.jpg?w=1200&amp;h=811&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1200w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSP.jpg?w=2000&amp;h=1352&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 2000w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 2060px) 100vw, 2060px\"><img width=\"2060\" height=\"1393\" src=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSPannotated.jpg?w=2060&amp;h=1393&amp;fit=clip&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\" alt=\"Two people are seated looking up into the night sky. Jupiter, M44, and Mars are indicated with text labels.\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSPannotated.jpg?w=2060&amp;h=1393&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 2060w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSPannotated.jpg?w=300&amp;h=203&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 300w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSPannotated.jpg?w=768&amp;h=519&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 768w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSPannotated.jpg?w=1024&amp;h=692&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1024w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSPannotated.jpg?w=1536&amp;h=1039&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1536w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSPannotated.jpg?w=2048&amp;h=1385&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 2048w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSPannotated.jpg?w=400&amp;h=270&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 400w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSPannotated.jpg?w=600&amp;h=406&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 600w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSPannotated.jpg?w=900&amp;h=609&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 900w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSPannotated.jpg?w=1200&amp;h=811&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1200w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSPannotated.jpg?w=2000&amp;h=1352&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2060px) 100vw, 2060px\"></p></div> <div> <p><strong>Explanation:</strong> <a href=\"https://earthsky.org/astronomy-essentials/everything-you-need-to-know-zodiacal-light-or-false-dusk\">Also known as the false dawn</a>, a luminous band of zodiacal light is captured in this dark night skyscape. The serene view was recorded just before the beginning of astronomical <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twilight\">twilight</a> during September's star party at the remote Hanle Dark Sky Reserve, Ladakh, India, planet Earth. At about 4,500 meters altitude, the dark sky reserve <a href=\"https://www.bbc.com/travel/article/20250829-the-himalayan-village-where-you-can-see-the-cosmos\">presents a haven</a> for hardy stargazing and astrophotography enthusiasts. While meteors streak through the night, bright planet Jupiter appears immersed in the faint zodiacal glow near the eastern horizon. <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/fap/image/2609/2026-09-09ZodiacalLightHSPannotated1024.jpg\">Follow the zodiacal band</a> toward the zenith to find open star cluster M44 and a yellowish tinged planet Mars near the center of the frame. In fact, <a href=\"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2020JE006509\">serendipitous</a> detections of interplanetary dust by NASA's Juno spacecraft suggest Mars itself is the source of dust that back scatters sunlight and creates <a href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/feature/goddard/2021/serendipitous-juno-spacecraft-detections-shatter-ideas-about-origin-of-zodiacal-light\">zodiacal light in planet Earth's night.</a></p><p><strong>APOD's main NASA site is <a href=\"https://asterisk.apod.com/viewtopic.php?t=45023\">moving</a>:</strong> From <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/\">apod.nasa.gov</a> to <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod\">science.nasa.gov/apod</a><br><strong>Tomorrow's picture: </strong><a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/fap/ap260920.html\">only sunny days</a></p></div> </div></div>",
